#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:76
msgid "Send burn-on-read messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/_static/badges/entry-adv.rst:7
msgid ""
"|plans-img-yellow| Available on `Entry and Enterprise Advanced "
"<https://mattermost.com/pricing/>`__ plans"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:81
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v11.3, burn-on-read messages stay concealed until "
"recipients reveal them. After revealing, the message is deleted for that "
"recipient when the timer expires. Burn-on-read messages can't be replied "
"to or edited. You can send burn-on-read messages unless your system admin"
" has :ref:`disabled the ability to do so <administration-guide/configure"
"/site-configuration-settings:enable burn-on-read messages>` in your "
"Mattermost instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:85
#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:93
msgid "Compose your message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:86
msgid ""
"Select the **Burn-on-read** |burn-on-read-icon| icon in the message "
"toolbar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:151
msgid "Burn on Read icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:91
msgid ""
"From Mattermost mobile v2.38.0, you can send burn-on-read messages from "
"the mobile app."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:94
msgid "Tap the **Burn-on-read** |burn-on-read-icon| icon in the message toolbar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:95
msgid "Tap **Send** |send-icon|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:97
msgid ""
"Recipients see a concealed placeholder with **Reveal**. After revealing, "
"a timer shows when the message will be deleted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:99
msgid ""
"As the message sender, hover over the **Burn-on-read** |burn-on-read-"
"icon| icon above the sent message to see how many recipients have read "
"the message. You can also delete the burn-on-read message for all "
"recipients before the timer expires by selecting the **Burn-on-read** "
"|burn-on-read-icon| icon above the sent message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:102
msgid "Draft messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:104
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v7.7, when composing new messages, it's easy to return to"
" a message in progress later, unless your system admin has :ref:`disabled"
" global drafts <administration-guide/configure/site-configuration-"
"settings:enable server syncing of message drafts>` in the System Console."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:106
msgid ""
"By default, message drafts are synchronized on the Mattermost server and "
"are accessible everywhere you access Mattermost, including a web browser "
"or the desktop app. Limit drafts to your current Mattermost client only "
"by going to **Settings > Advanced > Allow message drafts to sync with the"
" server** to disable draft synchronization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:110
msgid ""
"Draft messages are added to a **Drafts** view available at the top of the"
" channel sidebar."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:112
msgid "Global drafts makes it easy for you to find all messages in progress."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:118
msgid ""
"When composing a message, you can simply choose to complete it later. The"
" partially composed message is kept in the text field and an **Edit** "
"option |edit-icon| displays next to the channel name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../<rst_prolog>:141
msgid "Edit icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:120
msgid ""
"From Mattermost v10.5, you'll find local draft messages under **Drafts**."
" Drafts synchronized to the Mattermost server will be listed under "
"**Drafts** in a future mobile app release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/send-messages.rst:122
msgid ""
"You can sync a daft message by exiting the channel mid-way while "
"composing the message."
msgstr ""

